---
/**
 * Opportunity — Economics-lens concept at Single scale.
 * Opportunity cost of every allocation under scarcity.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Opportunity | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Economics lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Opportunity
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Opportunity cost of every allocation under scarcity.
					What is forgone when degrees of freedom are committed to one path instead of another.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Core concept under the Economics lens.
						Analogy, not isomorphism.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">What is given up.</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Opportunity</strong> is the value of the next-best alternative the Identity forgoes when it commits scarce degrees of freedom to one path.
					It is measured relative to the Metric Stem, weighted by Mass, and ranked by Preference under Ownership.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the Economics lens, Opportunity closes the Single scale.
					Scarcity makes choice necessary. Ownership attributes the scarce degrees of freedom to a subject.
					Preference ranks the ends. Opportunity names the cost of that ranking in the currency of forgone alternatives — including forgone future causal optionality and Stem coherence.
				</p>
				<p>
					Interaction expands the set of available alternatives, but the cost concept itself belongs to the Single Identity:
					it is always this Identity’s forgone path under its scarcity and its jurisdiction.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Opportunity is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Forgone alternative:</strong> the value of the next-best use of the same degrees of freedom.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Stem-relative cost:</strong> measured against the Metric Stem and Vision Gradient of the owning Identity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Bridge to Exchange:</strong> once Opportunity is legible, comparing own cost with another Identity’s Price becomes possible.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Causal-entropy sensitive:</strong> high opportunity cost often means high loss of future optionality or Stem coherence, not only lost output.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Opportunity is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a market Price.</strong>
						Price is an interactive signal. Opportunity is the Single Identity’s internal cost of its own allocation.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not only monetary.</strong>
						The forgone path can be attention, context depth, relationship, or future freedom.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not externalized by default.</strong>
						Shifting work to another Identity changes the opportunity profile; it does not erase it.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not identical with Scarcity.</strong>
						Scarcity is the condition of finitude. Opportunity is the cost of a concrete choice under that condition.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Make the next-best alternative explicit</strong> before large allocations.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Compare own Opportunity with external Price signals</strong> when deciding make-or-buy.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Protect high-Mass, high-optionality paths</strong> from silent dissipation.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Treat Stem-coherence loss</strong> as a first-class opportunity cost.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/30 p-6">
					<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/40 mb-3">Quick self-check</div>
					<ul class="space-y-3 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
						<li>What is the next-best use of the degrees of freedom about to be committed?</li>
						<li>Does the external Price undercut or exceed own Opportunity for this path?</li>
						<li>Which forgone alternative would most damage long-term causal optionality?</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Related</div>
					<p>
						Prior: Scarcity → Ownership → Preference.
						Next scale: <a href="/framework/exchange" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Exchange</a> (Interactive).
						Physics parallel: coherent velocity vs. dissipative motion along the Stem.
						Biology parallel: metabolic opportunity cost under finite energy.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/preference" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Preference</a>
					<a href="/framework/exchange" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Exchange</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
